Package: nova
Version: 0.1.0
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: binutils, libc6
Recommends: gcc
Maintainer: Nova Project <maintainers@nova-lang.org>
Homepage: https://github.com/nova-lang/nova
Description: Self-hosting Nova programming language compiler
 Nova is a self-hosting compiled language that targets x86-64 (Linux,
 Windows, macOS) and ARM64 (Linux, Android, iOS, Windows) without a
 libc dependency. It emits GAS-syntax assembly which is then handed
 off to the GNU binutils assembler and linker.
 .
 Highlights:
  * Single-binary toolchain (~700KB).
  * Two-stage self-hosting build (stage2 bit-equal to stage3).
  * Multiple codegen targets (Linux/Windows/macOS x86-64, ARM64,
    WASM/WASI, Windows ARM64).
  * Direct syscall runtime - no libc, no allocator, no GC.
 .
 This package installs the compiler binary to /usr/local/bin/nova,
 the manual page to /usr/share/man/man1/, and a curated set of
 example programs to /usr/share/doc/nova/examples/.
